{
  "$schema_note": "UI metadata layer for the Stage 3 Google Sheets staging bootstrap. It NEVER redefines sheet headers (those live only in config/sheets_contracts.json). It declares, per contract sheet+column: data validations (dropdowns sourced from a canonical enum) and checkboxes (canonically boolean fields). Column widths and number/date formats are derived deterministically from reusable semantic rules in n8n/lib/sheets_bootstrap_planner.js, not hand-listed here. Every dropdown resolves an enum_ref: 'taxonomy:<key>' reads config/taxonomy.json; 'canonical:<name>' reads canonical_enums below. Each canonical enum records its source. n8n/lib/sheets_contract_resolver.js fails if an enum_ref or a referenced column/sheet cannot be resolved. Add a new dropdown by pointing a column at an existing enum or adding a new canonical enum with its source.",
  "version": "sheets-ui-v1",

  "validation_strictness_policy": "strict=true rejects values outside the canonical list (closed, stable enums normalized by the workflows). strict=false shows the list as suggestions with a warning but accepts other values (legacy/alias-bearing columns, comma-lists, or columns that may hold historical values) so the bootstrap never rejects pre-existing data. Dropdowns and checkboxes are applied from row 2 downward; header cells (row 1) are never validated.",

